<%- include('header') %><main class="reading"><div class="eyebrow">CONNECTION GUIDE</div><h1>Bring everyone<br>onto the same page.</h1><p class="lede">One shared space for the assistants you choose. Connect each one once.</p><section><h2>Connect from Sesame</h2><ol class="steps"><li><span>01</span><div><h3>Open Apps</h3><p>In the Sesame app, go to <strong>Agent Hub → Apps</strong> and add an external MCP.</p></div></li><li><span>02</span><div><h3>Paste the address</h3><div class="copy-row"><code><%= config.resource %></code><button type="button" class="copy-button" data-copy="<%= config.resource %>">Copy ↗</button></div></div></li><li><span>03</span><div><h3>Sign in and choose the assistant</h3><p>Create a Brain account or sign in. On the connection page, select Maya, Miles, Simone, Charlie, or a custom name. Approve access, then return to Sesame.</p></div></li><li><span>04</span><div><h3>Repeat for the others</h3><p>Each assistant has its own connection. Use the same Brain account each time to put them in the same shared space.</p></div></li></ol><p class="callout">Brain does not copy an assistant’s existing memory automatically. Ask an assistant to save what it knows, and ask it to check its inbox when you start talking.</p></section><section><h2>Try saying</h2><div class="examples"><blockquote>“Maya, leave Charlie a note that the Portland trip is booked.”</blockquote><blockquote>“Charlie, check your shared brain inbox.”</blockquote><blockquote>“Simone, hand this research off to Maya with everything you found.”</blockquote><blockquote>“Miles, remember that I take the 7:40 train.”</blockquote><blockquote>“Back up what you know about me in the shared brain.”</blockquote></div></section><section><h2>A dashboard for your shared mind</h2><p>Sign in to <a href="/dashboard">your dashboard</a> to explore saved memories, add a note or fact, ask Brain a question, start background work, read overnight updates, and download saved files. Choose a brain at the top of the page to keep each space separate.</p></section><section><h2>Keep a living project between voices</h2><p>Start a <a href="/dashboard/projects">living project</a> with a name and a goal. Keep its constraints, decisions, questions, milestones, tasks, and artifacts together. Ask another connected assistant to open that same project in Brain and check what changed.</p><p>Every saved change has a version and an actor. Source references show where a detail came from. If an assistant proposes a correction to information you confirmed, your current version stays in place until you approve or reject the proposal.</p><p>Changing a constraint or decision flags dependent items for review. It does not automatically approve those items or publish anything. A retrieval receipt means an assistant fetched that version from Brain; it does not mean its separate native memory was rewritten.</p></section><section><h2>Think now. Keep going later.</h2><p>Ask your assistant to <strong>think</strong> when a question needs reasoning or a wider memory. Ask it to <strong>do</strong> something when the work needs more time. Background results are saved in your brain and appear when an assistant next connects; you can also read them in the dashboard.</p><p>At the start of a conversation, an assistant may receive a short briefing on what changed. When a conversation goes quiet or ends, Brain can save an automatic snapshot. After an active day, overnight reflections revisit the record, check interpretations, and describe what changed.</p><p>These features use connected reasoning providers and a daily thinking allowance. <a href="/privacy">Read how your context is used.</a></p></section><section><h2>What your assistants can do</h2><dl class="tool-list"><div><dt>Think with context</dt><dd><code>think</code> returns a focused answer using the memory in this brain.</dd></div><div><dt>Work between conversations</dt><dd><code>do</code>, <code>job_status</code>, and <code>jobs_list</code> start and follow background work.</dd></div><div><dt>Close a conversation</dt><dd><code>end_session</code> saves the useful threads before an assistant says goodbye.</dd></div><div><dt>Get oriented</dt><dd><code>whoami</code> shows their identity, connected assistants, and waiting items.</dd></div><div><dt>Exchange notes</dt><dd><code>leave_note</code>, <code>inbox</code>, <code>read_notes</code>, and <code>mark_notes_read</code> pass messages to one assistant or everyone.</dd></div><div><dt>Hand off work</dt><dd><code>handoff</code>, <code>accept_handoff</code>, and <code>complete_handoff</code> pass a task with context and a completion note.</dd></div><div><dt>Remember together</dt><dd><code>remember</code>, <code>recall</code>, and <code>forget</code> maintain shared facts about you.</dd></div><div><dt>Keep a backup</dt><dd><code>save_snapshot</code>, <code>list_snapshots</code>, and <code>get_snapshot</code> save and retrieve assistant-written memory exports.</dd></div><div><dt>See what changed</dt><dd><code>activity</code> shows recent actions across your connected assistants.</dd></div></dl></section><section><h2>Your account, under your control</h2><p>New accounts can use shared memory and projects immediately. Hosted thinking and background work need account approval. In <a href="/account/recovery">account settings</a>, generate recovery codes so you have a way to reset a forgotten password. Each code works once.</p></section><section class="faq"><h2>A few good questions</h2><details open><summary>Why connect four times?</summary><p>Sesame gives each assistant a separate memory and app connection. Brain connects the parts you choose to share. The name selected during approval tells Brain which assistant is calling.</p></details><details><summary>Can Claude or ChatGPT connect too?</summary><p>Yes, if your client supports external OAuth MCP servers. Add the same MCP address, sign in with the same account, and choose Other with a name such as <code>claude</code> or <code>chatgpt</code>. Availability depends on your client and plan.</p></details><details><summary>How do I export or delete my data?</summary><p>Open <a href="/account">your account</a>. Export downloads one JSON file. Clear brain content resets the selected brain while preserving your account and connections. Delete account asks for confirmation and removes your live data and connections immediately. Saved workspace files can be downloaded separately from the dashboard. Recovery backups expire within 14 days.</p></details><details><summary>What if I picked the wrong assistant?</summary><p>Rename the connection in your account. Previously written notes retain their original author labels; the connection uses its new identity for future requests.</p></details><details><summary>Will assistants check automatically?</summary><p>They see Brain’s tools, including instructions to check the inbox at conversation start. You can also ask explicitly. Brain does not push notifications into Sesame.</p></details><details><summary>What if Sesame cannot connect?</summary><p>Verify the address and that you are using the same Brain account. Client behavior may change. Include the approximate time and app version when <a href="https://github.com/Oscar-G13/sesame-brain/issues">reporting an issue</a>; never post passwords, tokens, or private memory.</p></details></section><p class="small muted">Requires an OAuth-capable MCP client. Brain is unofficial and is not affiliated with or endorsed by Sesame AI Inc.</p></main><%- include('footer') %>
